
# Cable Utilities

>  Don't Get Tangled

---
The &bCable Anchor&r, &bInverted Toggle Anchor&r, &bToggle Anchor&r, and &bLevel Emitter&r are all &6placed onto a cable&r and exist in the &asame block space&r. (Meaning in the same 1 block area). &bColored cables&r only connect to &acables of the same color&r, or &bFluix cables&r. 

{image:cottagewitch:textures/quest_images/ae2_cable.png width:250 height:230 align:1}

Using a &bCable Anchor&r on a cable will &aprevent any other cables from connecting&r on that side.

The &bToggle Anchor&r is similar to the &bCable Anchor&r, but &6powering it with redstone&r will &aallow another cable to connect&r. The &bInverted Toggle Anchor&r is the opposite, &aallowing an adjacent cable to connect by default&r &ounless&r &6powered by redstone&r.

The &bLevel Emitter&r will &aprovide a redstone signal based on configurable conditions&r. To access these, you can &6right click on the &bEmitter&r to access its interface. You can &adefine an item for the &bEmitter&r to monitor (such as a diamond), and &achoose what set of rules you would like it to use&r.

{image:cottagewitch:textures/quest_images/level_emitter_ui.png width:250 height:230 align:1}
            